{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Bounded completion recovery is unreachable for a step-budget exhaustion\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a].\n\n`CompletionAgentStep.run` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:426`) catches ONLY\n`UnretryableOutputError`, and only when `_is_token_exhaustion(exc)` holds. A step-budget exhaustion\nraises `LLMRunnerError` (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:95` builds it as `budget_err` with a\n`.diagnostic` attached), and per `src/rebar/llm/errors.py` `LLMRunnerError` is a strict ANCESTOR of\n`UnretryableOutputError` — so it never matches and the recovery never engages.\n\nConfirmed by experiment, with a control: a synthetic budget `LLMRunnerError` fed to\n`CompletionAgentStep.run` PROPAGATED and left `failure_diagnostic is None`; the control, an\n`UnretryableOutputError` truncation, ENTERED recovery.\n\nThis matters because bounded recovery is exactly the mechanism the failure needs. It isolates each\nexplicit criterion in a FRESH agentic history (so a loop cannot persist across criteria), converges\nthe evidence run at 16 run steps, and finishes with a tool-free structured finalizer — see\n`docs/llm-framework.md`. The error message printed to the operator says \"narrow the task\", and\nthis is the machinery that does exactly that, sitting unreachable one `except` clause away.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the `except` clause in `CompletionAgentStep.run` to also catch a step-budget exhaustion and\nroute it to the existing `_recover(...)` — the smallest change that makes the shipped machinery\nreachable. Budget exhaustion is identified as an `LLMRunnerError` carrying a step-budget\n`diagnostic` (the shape `interpret_failure` attaches at `structured_run.py:95-103`: a dict with\n`requests`/`tool_calls`/`request_limit` keys), not by message text — a typed-plus-diagnostic check,\nso unrelated `LLMRunnerError`s (e.g. config errors) keep propagating unchanged. The truncation path\nkeeps its exact current behaviour: `UnretryableOutputError` + `_is_token_exhaustion` still routes to\nthe same `_recover`. `_recover`'s own fail-closed guarantees are untouched — this ticket only adds\nthe missing entry edge. The budget diagnostic is preserved onto `self.failure_diagnostic` before\nrecovery so that if recovery ALSO fails, `raise_completion_workflow_failure` has the loop-vs-breadth\ncounters (the surfacing of those counters is [rebar:8b97-a0ca-82a4-4d4e]'s subject).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py` — the `except` spine of `CompletionAgentStep.run`\n  plus a small budget-exhaustion predicate beside `_is_token_exhaustion`.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py` — the tests below (extends the existing\n  suite for this class).\n\nOut of scope: what `tool_step_limit` does inside the evidence runs ([rebar:e1b1-859e-a7b4-48f2]);\nthe runaway detector/actuator ([rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]); sidecar emission\n([rebar:8b97-a0ca-82a4-4d4e]).\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py -q\n\nHappy path: a budget `LLMRunnerError` (with the step-budget diagnostic) from the primary step enters\nrecovery and produces a verdict. Edge: an `LLMRunnerError` WITHOUT the budget diagnostic still\npropagates (negative control); the truncation path is regression-pinned. Failure path: recovery that\ncannot produce full criterion coverage still fails closed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a step-budget exhaustion (`LLMRunnerError` carrying the step-budget diagnostic) routes into the\n      bounded per-criterion recovery instead of propagating; verified by a test driving it end to end\n      through `CompletionAgentStep.run` with a fake runner and asserting recovery ran and produced a\n      verdict\n- [ ] an `LLMRunnerError` without the step-budget diagnostic still propagates unchanged (the catch is\n      typed + diagnostic-shaped, not blanket); verified by a negative-control test\n- [ ] the truncation path keeps its current behaviour exactly (`UnretryableOutputError` +\n      `_is_token_exhaustion` -> recovery; non-exhaustion `UnretryableOutputError` propagates);\n      regression-pinned by the existing tests passing unmodified\n- [ ] recovery still fails CLOSED when it cannot produce full criterion coverage — this must never\n      become a route to an unearned PASS; verified by a test where recovery's preconditions fail and\n      the step still raises\n- [ ] when recovery also fails, the original budget diagnostic is preserved on\n      `self.failure_diagnostic` (not lost); verified by a test asserting the diagnostic's\n      `requests`/`tool_calls` counters survive"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785955008473311001,"uuid":"61298d86-22f3-4ae9-a57d-c65522a65a89"}